=== 2D SCREEN BUFFER [80x24] ===
--- TEXT MATRIX ---
00: |                                                                                |
01: |┃ /btw What is the difference between Elm architecture and standard             |
02: |┃ Bubbletea?                                                                    |
03: |┃                                                                               |
04: |┃   The Elm Architecture in Bubbletea                                           |
05: |┃                                                                               |
06: |┃   In standard object-oriented UI frameworks, components mutate their own      |
07: |┃   state directly. In Bubbletea:                                               |
08: |┃                                                                               |
09: |┃   1. Model: Pure representation of component data and view state.             |
10: |┃   2. View: Pure projection of Model into a string representation.             |
11: |┃   3. Update: Pure reducer handling incoming messages and returning the        |
12: |┃   updated Model with optional asynchronous tea.Cmd.                           |
13: |┃                                                                               |
14: |┃   Key Principles:                                                             |
15: |┃                                                                               |
16: |┃   • Single source of truth.                                                   |
17: |┃   • Decoupled asynchronous side-effects.                                      |
18: |┃   • Deterministic, easily testable UI transitions.                            |
19: |┃                                                                               |
20: |┃ Tab to collapse · Enter/Esc to dismiss                                        |
21: |                                                                                |
22: |Storybook tip: Press Tab to toggle card expansion interactively                 |
23: |                                                                                |
